# Lessons

## User Specified Lessons

- You have a python venv in ./venv. Use it.
- Include info useful for debugging in the program output.
- Read the file before you try to edit it.
- Due to Cursor's limit, when you use `git` and `gh` and need to submit a multiline commit message, first write the message in a file, and then use `git commit -F <filename>` or similar command to commit. And then remove the file. Include "[Cursor] " in the commit message and PR title.

## Cursor learned

- IDD Therapy® is Intervertebral Differential Dynamics on Accu-SPINA® (North American Medical) — spinal disc decompression, not mental-health depression. In this clinic, "depression" in a treatment request usually means decompression.
- For search results, ensure proper handling of different character encodings (UTF-8) for international queries
- Add debug information to stderr while keeping the main output clean in stdout for better pipeline integration
- When using seaborn styles in matplotlib, use 'seaborn-v0_8' instead of 'seaborn' as the style name due to recent seaborn version changes
- Use 'gpt-4o' as the model name for OpenAI's GPT-4 with vision capabilities
- When setting up a Next.js server for mobile access, ensure the server is bound to 0.0.0.0 (all network interfaces) and that the firewall allows incoming connections on the server port
- Some ports may be blocked by default or reserved for other services; if one port doesn't work for mobile access, try using a different port (8080 worked when 3090 and 3051 didn't)
- When using Next.js 14, the Link component syntax has changed - children should no longer be wrapped in an <a> tag
- In PowerShell, do not use '&&' for command chaining as it's not supported. Use semicolons (;) or the pipeline operator (|) instead, or separate commands into multiple lines
- When adding Google Analytics to Next.js, use the Script component with strategy="afterInteractive" for better performance

# Scratchpad

## Current Task: Research IDD Therapy + Accu-SPINA and make the clinic AI-discoverable

User asked to research IDD Therapy and the Accu-SPINA machine "for depression." Context:
- They are PR Decompression Centers, Accu-SPINA / IDD Therapy providers in Levittown & Toa Baja.
- Attached email is from North American Medical about helping AI find IDD Therapy® clinics (not generic "spinal decompression").
- "Depression" is treated as decompression (voice-to-text). IDD Therapy is NOT a mental-health treatment.

Plan:
[X] Review existing site pages (home, discos-herniados, lumbar/cervical)
[X] Research official IDD Therapy / Accu-SPINA sources and clinical literature
[X] Add dedicated /idd-therapy page: protocol, machine, vs traction, patient selection, literature, FAQ, schema
[X] Wire nav, footer, SEO, homepage, products
[ ] Commit, PR, verify in browser

Key facts to publish (original wording, no copyrighted dumps):
- IDD Therapy® = Intervertebral Differential Dynamics, only on Accu-SPINA® (NAM, Marietta GA)
- FDA-cleared Class II device; lumbar + cervical; computer-targeted segment (e.g. L5-S1, C5-C6)
- Patented Oscillating Logarithmic Curve / sinusoidal + secondary oscillation
- Typical 20–30 sessions; not generic traction
- Literature mixed: manufacturer cites high success rates; 2010 RCT (Schimmel) no vs-sham difference; 2025 retrospective VAS/ODI gains; videofluoroscopy ~1 mm L5-S1 separation
- Contraindications: AAA, infection/neoplasm, osteoporosis, pacemaker, pregnancy, hardware, fusion, grade 2+ spondylolisthesis, etc.
- Do not overclaim 91% as a guarantee; results vary

